# TP: Isolated AGDF test mode for native Codex Desktop click tests

Status: draft
Gate: TP
Gate approval: open
Based on: SD
Date: 2026-11-22
Owner: AGDF Core and Codex integration maintainers
Traceability contract: criteria-chain-v1
Planning Decisions contract: tp-decisions-v1

## 1. Task List

Implement the [approved solution design](SD.md) for the six criteria in the [PRD](PRD.md). A fixture is a disposable Run in the isolated profile. Its only work is a status read and a reply containing the case marker.

| task_id | Task | Owner | Dependencies |
|---|---|---|---|
| T-001 | Extend local test setup to create the isolated workspace and explicit fixture designation. Record canonical roots, profile and activation identity, installed generation and the exact Run, revision, operation and case marker. Add a read-only preflight and deliberate deactivation. | Codex integration | Approved SD and Brownfield Analysis before code changes |
| T-002 | Implement one server-side test-scope decision at both entry points. Resolve actual profile and package identity independently on each route, require a shared admission root, and recheck eligibility and canonical binding on reserve, publish and claim. Cover deactivation and predecessor continuity. | AGDF Core and Codex integration | T-001 |
| T-003 | Use the existing per-Run admission service and hook association for fixture requests. Return the fixed status-read task only to the winning dispatch. Preserve pending work on reopen, cancellation, interruption and upgrade. Add a case-scoped timing checkpoint for repeatable observation in the isolated test harness. | AGDF Core and Codex integration | T-002 |
| T-004 | Present the test scope, named fixture, current state, blocker and available action in the existing Companion. Preserve keyboard focus on refresh. Show the candidate and case in details. Implement redacted case capture from the actual sources and label unavailable observations. | Companion UI and Codex integration | T-002 and T-003 |
| T-005 | Extend the existing Core, MCP, UI and built-browser suites. Verify packaging of the same sources, exercise ordinary use and invalid contexts, and record per-route counts and source identity before the first manual click. | AGDF integration and QA | T-001 through T-004 |
| T-006 | Install the identified candidate in the isolated profile, perform the native cases below, review case-local evidence, settle eligible fixtures and hand the records to the linked continuation Run for assessment. | Desktop test maintainer and QA | T-005 and matched preflight on both installed routes |

